Modifications: reduced to 64-bit arithmetic DPF; replaced cryptoTools block/AES
with EMP; replaced SCI multiplexer/comms with two-direction IKNP OT sharing
adapters; added an OT-based ripple-carry arithmetic-to-Boolean converter;
removed globals and unrelated applications; added two-process correctness tests.
This is an adapted extraction, not an unchanged copy or a performance-equivalent
implementation of the upstream backend.

Bundled EMP-OT files: ot.h, cot.h, co.h, iknp.h, unchanged from tag 0.2.4,
commit d5f4fc89433c1e391de16c209bcca1a08755507b.
Copyright (c) 2018 Xiao Wang. MIT license in vendor/emp-ot/LICENSE.

EMP-Tool is an external local dependency, not included in this archive.

2026-09-21 extension: shared-tree two-coordinate additive uint64 payloads,
domain-separated leaf PRF conversion, and pruned public-prefix evaluation.
The user's supplied evalAll cGGM/ET code informed traversal design; ordinary
GGM expansion and correction semantics are retained. This is not a KH-PRF
implementation or a complete RSIA.Update protocol.

LWR extension: independently implemented the inner-product/high-bit truncation
structure inspected in CPS4AI/OpenSFSS sfss.h at
9f7d3dafec3865a6f815f9ad1974d9291192d4e4. Uses EMP CRH, 512 coefficients in
Z/(2^128), and output in Z/(2^64). Adds product-group DPF payloads and 128-bit
OT MUX. This implements approximate key homomorphism, not exact RSIA.Update.
